+
+    // The measured chain of the cloud boot is two notices far apart: the first
+    // pop-up answers an Enter within seconds of the window being live, but the
+    // Destiny 2 splash that says "PRESS ENTER TO PLAY" only arrives ~135 s
+    // after that press, and the enter clock's follow-up answers 5 s apart run
+    // the presses out long before it. Measured on the r0.67 board: one Enter at
+    // +60 s answered the consent notice and launched the game (the splash was
+    // witness in the streamer's own frame dumps), while the 12 presses 13 s
+    // apart that followed closed the host's own windows and left a bare
+    // desktop. So the play press is a clock of its own, armed far later and
+    // answering once: OPENNOW_PLAY_ENTER_MS says when, OPENNOW_PLAY_ENTER_TIMES
+    // (1 when unset) how many, OPENNOW_PLAY_ENTER_HOLD_MS (150 when unset) how
